---
title: ISA-95 Part 3 Operations Management - Request, Schedule, Response (mapped to MES AI)
---
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor ERP as ERP (SAP / Oracle)
    participant Req as Operations Request<br/>(ProductionOrder)
    participant Def as Operations Definition<br/>(ProcessRoute + RouteSteps)
    participant Sched as Operations Schedule<br/>(Dispatch Engine)
    participant Exec as Segment Execution<br/>(WIP Service + Equipment)
    participant Resp as Operations Response<br/>(Unit/LotHistory)
    participant Mat as Material Actuals<br/>(Inventory + Genealogy)
    participant Out as ERP Outbound Queue

    ERP->>Req: Release order (product, qty, due date)
    Req->>Def: Resolve route (order.route_id → default → first)
    Def-->>Req: ProcessRoute + ordered RouteSteps

    Note over Req,Sched: One Operations Request Segment<br/>Requirement per RouteStep

    Req->>Sched: Evaluate next segment (get_next_step)
    Sched->>Sched: Apply StepTransitions<br/>(disposition / on_pass / on_fail / always)
    Sched-->>Req: Target RouteStep (process segment)

    Req->>Sched: Evaluate dispatch options
    Sched->>Sched: Filter Equipment by<br/>availability + material setup + capacity
    Sched->>Sched: Rank by strategy<br/>(first_available / shortest_queue / ...)
    Sched-->>Exec: Assigned Equipment (inside a WorkCell)

    Exec->>Resp: Open UnitHistory / LotHistory<br/>(entered_at, step_id, equipment_id)
    Exec->>Mat: Consume input Lot<br/>(decrement inventory balance)
    Mat-->>Exec: Consumption recorded + genealogy edge
    Exec->>Exec: Collect StepParameter values<br/>(data collection)
    Exec->>Mat: Produce output Lot / increment sub-lot qty
    Exec->>Resp: Close history row<br/>(exited_at, result = pass/fail/rework)

    alt Result requires non-linear routing
        Resp->>Sched: Re-evaluate with result + disposition
        Sched-->>Req: Route to rework / MRB / scrap segment
    else Last segment completed
        Resp->>Req: Increment completed count<br/>(order progress)
    end

    Req->>Out: Emit WIP confirmation / goods receipt
    Out->>ERP: ERP outbound message<br/>(operation confirmation / GR)
